Kafka Connect and CDC ⭐⭐
What is Kafka Connect?
Kafka Connect integrates Kafka with external systems through reusable connectors.
Source connector: Moves data into Kafka.
Sink connector: Moves data from Kafka to an external destination.
What is CDC?
Change Data Capture identifies changes in a database, such as inserts, updates, and deletes.
A CDC tool such as Debezium can publish these changes to Kafka.
Example architecture:

Source Database
       |
       v
 CDC Tool / Connector
       |
       v
      Kafka
       |
       v
 Consumer / Sink Connector
       |
       v
    Data Lake


Interview answer:
CDC captures changes from a source database and makes them available to downstream systems. Kafka can transport these change events, while consumers or sink connectors deliver them to destinations such as a data lake or analytical database.




Guarantee
Meaning
At-most-once
An event is processed zero or one time; it may be lost from the processing perspective

At-least-once
An event may be processed more than once

Exactly-once
A defined processing operation produces one effective result within its supported scope

Most important takeaway: At-least-once processing can produce duplicates, so downstream systems may need idempotency.

Interview answer:
At-least-once processing helps avoid losing events but can lead to duplicates after failures. Exactly-once semantics aim to avoid duplicate effects within a defined processing boundary and require appropriate configuration and application design.